x754 call open x753 6
x755 write x754 4
x756 write x755 2
x757 text "cm"
x758 puts x756 x757
x759 write x758 2
x760 text "# a view of clamp, then a reply that fixes the upper bound\n"
x761 puts x759 x760
x762 call close x761 
x763 write x762 2
x764 text "e0 fn clamp u32 u32 u32 -> u32\nlo lt p0 p1\nhi lt p2 p0\na select lo p1 p0\nr select hi p2 a\nret r\n\n"
x765 puts x763 x764
x766 call open x765 6
x767 write x766 4
x768 write x767 2
x769 text "cm"
x770 puts x768 x769
x771 write x770 2
x772 text "# reply\n"
x773 puts x771 x772
x774 call close x773 
x775 write x774 2
x776 text "e0\nhi lt p2 a\nr select hi p2 a"
x777 puts x775 x776
x778 call close x777 
x779 call close x778 
x780 call close x779 
x781 call open x780 13
x782 write x781 4
x783 write x782 1
x784 text "diagnostics"
x785 puts x783 x784
x786 call open x785 11
x787 write x786 2
x788 text "Diagnostics"
x789 puts x787 x788
x790 call close x789 
x791 call open x790 2
x792 write x791 2
x793 text "Every rejection carries a stable code (parse, type, structure, handle, revision, limit), what was expected, what was seen, and the one fix that resolves it. The compiler never guesses: a reply that is ambiguous is rejected with the fix, not applied approximately."
x794 puts x792 x793
x795 call close x794 
x796 call close x795 
ret x796
end

fn sec_run io -> io
